    {
      "title": "‘Serious incident’ at Alberta military base causes deaths and injuries, Canada officials say",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
      "description": "<p>Patients being taken to hospitals in Edmonton as Wainwright ‘completely overwhelmed’ by number of injuries, local doctor says </p><p>People have been killed and injured after an incident at one of Canada’s busiest military training bases in Alberta caused a large fire, Canada’s defence minister said Saturday.</p><p>“I’m saddened to share that there have been both fatalities and injuries as a result of an incident on the base,” defence minister David McGuinty said at a press conference on Saturday night.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-18T02:50:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "Deadly ‘Incident’ at Canadian Forces Base Wainwright Sparks Fire",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/17/world/canada/fire-canadian-army-base-wainwright.html",
      "description": "The defense minister said people were killed and injured at a base in Alberta, but officials did not offer details on the cause.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-18T14:05:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Serious incident caused major fire at military base in Alberta: Canada's PM",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/serious-incident-caused-major-fire-at-military-base-in-alberta-canada-s-pm-126101800055_1.html",
      "description": "Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said that a \"serious incident\" caused a major fire at a military base in Alberta.\n\"A serious incident creating a major fire has occurred at CFB Wainwright, in Alberta,\" Carney said on Saturday in a social media post.\n\"Our thoughts are with all the brave women and men affected,\" he said.\nCarney said the federal government was working closely with Alberta officials and local authorities. He said he and Alberta Premier Danielle Smith were in close contact, as were their ministers and officials.\nCarney did not provide details about what caused the fire or whether anyone was injured.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
